    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "Identify the parts of $6p-5q-13$.\n(a) List the terms and the pronumerals.\n(b) State the coefficient of $p$ and the coefficient of $q$.\n(c) Identify the constant term.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Treat each subtraction as adding a negative.\n$6p-5q-13=6p+(-5q)+(-13)$\nThe terms are $6p$, $-5q$ and $-13$. The pronumerals are $p$ and $q$.\n(b) The coefficient of $p$ is $6$; the coefficient of $q$ is $-5$.\n(c) The constant term is $-13$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For the expression $\\frac{t}{4}-u+9$:\n(a) state the coefficient of $t$\n(b) state the coefficient of $u$\n(c) list all the terms.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $\\frac{t}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}t$, so the coefficient of $t$ is $\\frac{1}{4}$.\n(b) $-u=(-1)u$, so the coefficient of $u$ is $-1$.\n(c) $\\frac{t}{4}-u+9=\\frac{t}{4}+(-u)+9$\nThe terms are $\\frac{t}{4}$, $-u$ and $9$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For the expression $a-6b$:\n(a) list the terms\n(b) state the coefficient of $a$\n(c) identify the constant term.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $a-6b=a+(-6b)$, so the terms are $a$ and $-6b$.\n(b) $a=1a$, so the coefficient of $a$ is $1$.\n(c) Both terms contain a pronumeral. There is no separate number term, so the constant term is $0$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "State the coefficient of $p$ in $4q-\\frac{5p}{9}-16$.",
        "solution_text": "Treat subtraction as adding a negative.\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}4q-\\frac{5p}{9}-16\\\\&=4q+\\left(-\\frac{5p}{9}\\right)+(-16)\\\\&=4q+\\left(-\\frac{5}{9}\\right)p+(-16)\\end{aligned}$\nThe coefficient of $p$ is $-\\frac{5}{9}$."
      }
    ],
